---
// Story 1-6. Group classes — KEPT but deliberately MINIMAL and DEMOTED (A1).
//
// Findable, not front. Keegan is not driving traffic here and it is out of the
// launch nav; someone may still book, so the page has to be correct and
// complete, just not competing with the main service page for attention.
//
// ⚠️ THE CLASS TIME IS NAMED, AND IT IS ALWAYS PAIRED WITH THE BOOKING CHECK.
// RESOLVED (SM-9, Keegan 2026-07-31): the handstand class is SATURDAY 10-11am.
// The old site contradicted itself — /services/group-classes/ said "Saturday
// 10am" and /handstand-coaching/ said "Sunday 11am", both live simultaneously.
// Saturday was the correct one.
//
// 🔴 BUT NEVER PUBLISH THE TIME BARE. Keegan's own words: "its a low priority
// and i cancel it a lot due to low numbers atm." A fixed advertised time on a
// frequently-cancelled class recreates precisely the failure this project just
// spent a day removing from his opening hours — someone reads a time, turns up,
// and nothing is there. So the page names the time AND sends the reader to the
// booking page to confirm the week's session. The BOOKABLE STATE is the source
// of truth, not this page; same principle as hours coming from Cliniko rather
// than being hand-typed. If the class is ever paused, drop the time and keep the
// booking link — a one-line edit, not a redesign.
//
// ✅ THE MOBILITY CLASS TIME IS NOW CONFIRMED TOO: Wednesday 6-7pm, from Keegan
// on 2026-08-01. That CORROBORATES the 2026-07-20 capture rather than trusting
// it — the capture said "Wednesdays 6pm" but it came from the site being
// replaced, so it was held unpublished until a human confirmed it independently.
// Both class times on this page are now published, and both are paired with the
// booking check.
//
// ~~OPS PRECONDITION: the Mobility & Flexibility Group Class has NO bookable
// sessions scheduled in Cliniko~~ — STALE, corrected here 2026-07-31 because
// leaving it would contradict the class time this page now publishes. Quinn
// measured the real datepicker month by month (QN-1): mobility has 3 bookable
// days in August and 2 in September, handstand 3 and 1. Keegan has scheduled
// sessions since the note was written.
//
// The underlying warning is still worth keeping in spirit: class availability is
// Keegan-managed and CAN return to zero, which is exactly why every class time on
// this page is paired with "check the booking page" rather than standing alone.
// The same stale note still sits in src/data/services.json and is SM-12's to fix.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BookCta from '../../components/BookCta.astro';
import { service } from '../../lib/schema.mjs';
import { SITE_URL } from '../../lib/site-env.mjs';
import business from '../../data/business.json' with { type: 'json' };
import classBands from '../../assets/site/Group-Nordics-scaled.jpg';
import classRoom from '../../assets/site/Keegan-demonstrating.jpeg';
// Story 1-16 hero ground. A class participant mid-drill, from the gym rather
// than the studio — the setting the reader is being invited into.
import heroClass from '../../assets/site/IMG_1641.jpg';

// Bumped 2026-08-01: both class times added after Keegan confirmed them.
const LAST_CHANGED = new Date('2026-08-01T00:00:00+10:00');

// G-8 — Service with NO offers node. Cliniko has no billable item for the
// classes, so compact() drops offers rather than publishing a price the booking
// system cannot honour. The $20 is stated in the page text, where it is a fact
// about the class rather than a machine-readable offer Cliniko would have to
// back.
const SERVICE_NODE = service(SITE_URL, 'group-class');
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Group Classes, Northern Beaches | ${business.name}`}
  description="Weekly mobility, flexibility and handstand classes at Just Train Gym, Cromer. $20 per class, one hour, all levels welcome. A low-commitment way to start."
  updated={LAST_CHANGED}
>
  <script slot="head-jsonld" type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(SERVICE_NODE)} />

  {/* Story 1-16. The inner-page hero. The photograph is blurred and dimmed
      into a ground rather than shown as a picture, which is what makes the
      orange headline legible over it — see the measured note on .hero in
      BaseLayout. Decorative in that state, hence empty alt + aria-hidden. */}
  <section class="hero hero--page">
    <Image
      src={heroClass}
      alt=""
      aria-hidden="true"
      widths={[768, 1280, 1920]}
      sizes="100vw"
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <h1>Group classes</h1>
      <p class="lead">
    Two weekly classes at Just Train Gym in Cromer, $20 each, one hour. A low-barrier way to
    sample the same methods I use one-to-one, and both welcome complete beginners.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Image
    src={classBands}
    alt="Four people kneeling on mats in a mirrored studio, leaning back and holding resistance bands overhead during a group mobility class"
    widths={[480, 800]}
    sizes="(max-width: 44rem) 100vw, 24rem"
    class="page-img tall"
  />

  <h2>What happens in the mobility and flexibility class?</h2>
  {/* Keegan confirmed Wednesday 6-7pm on 2026-08-01, which corroborates the
      2026-07-20 capture rather than relying on it.

      ⚠️ NOTE THE WORDING IS NOT THE SAME AS THE HANDSTAND BLOCK BELOW, ON
      PURPOSE. That one says "numbers are small and I do sometimes cancel",
      which are Keegan's own words about the HANDSTAND class specifically. He
      has said nothing of the kind about this one, and copying the caveat across
      would put a discouraging claim in his mouth about a class he may well run
      reliably. The booking-check pointer still applies to both, because
      availability is Keegan-managed in Cliniko either way. */}
  <p class="class-time">
    <strong>Wednesdays, 6&ndash;7pm</strong> at Just Train Gym, Cromer. Check the booking page for
    the next session.
  </p>
  <p>
    A general warm-up, then 5 to 6 targeted drills covering the major muscle groups of the lower
    body. Each class is designed for all levels, with different levels of each exercise offered so
    you can tailor it to yourself.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some exercises involve weights or other tools like resistance bands to adjust the difficulty to
    your individual level. Some will also be prescribed based on basic mobility tests, so you get a
    personalised experience inside a group setting. If you have always wanted to touch your toes or
    be comfortable in a squat, but only have the time or funds to chip away at it for an hour each
    week, this class is for you.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What do I need?</strong> A yoga mat, foam roller or massage ball, and a towel are
    recommended, although I often have a spare or two if you don’t have one.
  </p>
  <BookCta slug="group-class" label="Reserve a spot in the mobility class" />

  <h2>What happens in the handstand class?</h2>
  <p class="class-time">
    <strong>Saturdays, 10&ndash;11am</strong> at Just Train Gym, Cromer. Numbers are small and I do
    sometimes cancel, so check the booking page for this week&rsquo;s session before you come.
  </p>
  <p>
    It takes you from never going upside down to your first 10-second hold and beyond. The class is
    designed for complete beginners and intermediate students, focusing on proper technique and
    time-tested drills that build the strength and control to reliably stay upside down.
  </p>
  <p>
    These classes are community focused and designed to get you to a level where you can join the
    handstand meetups I organise around the Northern Beaches. Hand balancing is usually a solitary
    practice, and the meetups turn it into a group activity where we share knowledge and cheer each
    other on.
  </p>
  <BookCta slug="handstand-class" label="Reserve a spot in the handstand class" />
  <p>
    <a href="/services/handstand/">One-to-one handstand coaching</a> is on its own page.
  </p>

  <Image
    src={classRoom}
    alt="A group class at Just Train Gym in Cromer, participants standing on mats while Keegan demonstrates a hinge with a weighted bag"
    widths={[480, 800]}
    sizes="(max-width: 44rem) 100vw, 44rem"
    class="page-img"
  />

  {/* LN-6 / 1-15 section rhythm. The page's one band, on the block a reader
      scrolling for a practical answer is actually hunting for: when, where, how
      much. Lifting it out of the column is what stops it reading as the seventh
      identical section down the page. */}
  <section class="band">
    <h2>When and where do the classes run?</h2>
    <p>
      Mobility and flexibility runs Wednesdays 6&ndash;7pm, handstands Saturdays 10&ndash;11am, both
      at Just Train Gym in Cromer. Classes are scheduled a few weeks at a time, so the booking page
      is the place to confirm the next actual session.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/contact/">Open the booking page</a> to see what is currently available.
    </p>
  </section>

  <h2>Do you run workshops instead?</h2>
  <p>
    Yes, if you run a business with a space and a member group. Workshops are stand-alone deep dives
    into a single skill: handstands, pancake, front splits, side splits, back bends, or arms-overhead
    full flexion. Each is tailor made, and skills are modular so several can be combined into a
    longer session.
  </p>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> to talk about running one in your
    space.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to next?</h2>
  <ul class="next-links">
    <li><a href="/contact/">Book a class or an appointment</a></li>
    <li><a href="/services/chiropractic-treatment/">Chiropractic &amp; Movement</a> — the one-to-one work</li>
    <li><a href="/services/">Services and pricing</a></li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }
  /* SM-9. The time and the "check before you come" live in ONE block on
     purpose. Splitting them would let a skim-reader take the time and miss the
     caveat, which is the whole failure mode this framing exists to prevent. */
  .class-time {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--ml-rule);
    padding-left: 0.9rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  .next-links {
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }
  .next-links li {
    margin: 0.35rem 0;
  }
</style>
